    "https://www.luther.edu/offices/hr/careers": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers at Luther | Luther College Skip to Navigation Skip to Search Skip to Cookie Banner Skip to Main Content Skip to Footer Links Request Information Visit Apply Information For Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Families Give Today Search Luther College Menu Academics Admission & Aid Athletics Music Student Life Request Information Visit Apply Give Today Information For Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Families Search Enter keywords below. Frequently searched keywords: Vehicle Registration & Parking Academic Calendar Housing & Dining Book Shop Contact Information Library Close Search Home > Offices > Human Resources > Careers at Luther Menu Menu Careers at Luther Employee Benefits Employee Resources Forms Luther Works / Work Study Safety & Risk Management Human Resources Staff Home > Offices > Human Resources > Careers at Luther Human Resources Human Resources Main 25 700 College Drive Decorah, Iowa 52101 hr@luther.edu Phone: 563-387-1134 Fax: 563-387-1391 Careers at Luther Luther is a place where students can learn actively, live purposefully, and lead courageously for a lifetime of impact. We strive to be a community where students, faculty, and staff are enlivened and transformed by encounters with one another, by the exchange of ideas, and by the life of faith and learning. We are excited that you are considering Luther as the next step in your career. See the links below for information about working for Luther College and living in beautiful Decorah, Iowa. Apply for Jobs Open Positions Life at Luther College Living in Decorah Inclusivity and Belonging at Luther Employee Benefits Summary Candidate Information and Resources Background and Driving Screenings Background Check Background checks are conducted on all new staff and faculty at Luther College. If you have been asked to complete a background check as a new employee, please visit the Luther on-line candidate verification center website provided to start the process. Driver Screening If you will drive a Luther vehicle, or are a prospective employee who is required to drive by their position, please download and complete the driver application (at the end of the Handbook) which will allow us to check your motor vehicle report. The Vehicle Use Handbook can be accessed here and is required to be read before a Luther vehicle is driven. Nondiscrimination Statement “It is the policy of Luther College to provide equal educational opportunities and equal access to facilities for all qualified persons. The College does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, and activities on the basis of age, color, creed, disability, ethnicity, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law. Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 – No person in the United States shall, on the basis of sex, be excluded from participation in, be denied the benefits of, or be subjected to discrimination under any education program or activity receiving Federal financial assistance.” Questions regarding this policy or the complete Title IX Policy or Bias Incident, Hate Act, Hate Crime, Discrimination, and Harassment Policy should be directed to Robert Clay, Title IX Coordinator, 563-387-1825, titleix@luther.edu, 700 College Drive, Decorah, Iowa 52101. Questions regarding Title IX may also be referred to the U.S. Department of Education’s Office for Civil Rights, 800-421-3481, OCR@ed.gov, http://www.ed.gov/ocr. Hiring Process Luther College has a policy on staff recruitment to ensure that consistent guidelines are followed as exempt and non-exempt staff are hired. Consistent guidelines are necessary to ensure compliance issues are followed regarding federal, state, and local regulations. Human Resources Human Resources Main 25 700 College Drive Decorah, Iowa 52101 hr@luther.edu Phone: 563-387-1134 Fax: 563-387-1391 Luther College 700 College Drive Decorah, Iowa 52101 USA Maps & Directions Contact Us About Luther Book Shop Departments Directory Events Jobs at Luther News Offices Our Mission Virtual Tour Maps & Directions Contact Us It is the policy of Luther College to provide equal educational opportunities and equal access to facilities for all qualified persons. The college does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, and activities on the basis of age, color, creed, disability, ethnicity, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law. Back to Top Emergency Information Privacy Statement Title IX Report a Website Problem © LUTHER COLLEGE. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED."
